#  gdisable_driver.icn -- the grading vehicle for gprocs/gdisable.icn: it links gdisable and exercises gdisable(),
#  which assigns 1 to every graphics procedure name it lists; under this oracle (built without graphics) none of
#  those names is a builtin, so each is an undeclared identifier -- a local of gdisable -- and the assignments
#  simply complete, gdisable() returns &null, and the same names seen from main are still &null afterwards.
#  NOT exercised: nothing -- gdisable is the module's only procedure (its effect of disabling real graphics
#  builtins needs a graphics-enabled Icon, which this oracle is not).
link gdisable
procedure main()
   write("gdisable() returned ", image(gdisable()));
   write("again: ", image(gdisable()));
   write("DrawLine in main: ", image(DrawLine));
   write("WAttrib in main: ", image(WAttrib));
   write("done");
end
